course: dictionary
lesson: 4182
title: Goldilocks: just right
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words start as names. Goldilocks is a girl in an old fairy tale, and her name is now used to mean "just right". «Life as we know it needs liquid water, so scientists look for planets in the "Goldilocks zone", not too hot and not too cold, like Goldilocks' porridge.» The clue is "not too hot and not too cold", so the zone must be the just-right area.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Porridge that is too hot burns your mouth, and porridge that is too cold is no good. So a planet in the Goldilocks zone is neither too hot nor too cold, which fits "just right" perfectly.
explain: Notice the capital letter and the quotation marks. "Goldilocks" with a capital G can be the girl in the tale, but in science it names a special area in space. Ask yourself: is this about a girl in a story, or about something being just right?
fact: Goldilocks is a girl in the fairy tale «Goldilocks and the Three Bears».
fact: In the tale, she tries the bears' porridge, chairs and beds and likes the ones that are «just right».
fact: Informally, «Goldilocks» can describe something that is not too much and not too little, but just right.
fact: The Goldilocks zone is the area around a star where a planet is neither too hot nor too cold for liquid water.
fact: Scientists look for planets in the Goldilocks zone because liquid water matters for life as we know it.
exercise: In the fairy tale, Goldilocks likes the porridge, chairs and beds that are... | Too cold | Too hot | *Just right | Too big
exercise: «Scientists look for planets in the "Goldilocks zone".» What is the Goldilocks zone? | A bowl of porridge in a fairy tale | *An area around a star where a planet is neither too hot nor too cold for liquid water | A cold, dark part of space with no stars | A hot place where it is always sunny
exercise: Mia says, «We need a Goldilocks amount of sugar in the cake.» What does she mean? | *Not too much and not too little | Nothing at all | A bear's sugar bowl | Far too much sugar
test: Which word describes something that is not too much and not too little? | Frozen | Enormous | *Goldilocks | Dark
test: Why do scientists look for planets in the Goldilocks zone? | *Because liquid water can exist there | Because it is the hottest place in space | Because the planets are very small | Because Goldilocks lives there
exam: What does «Goldilocks» mean in «a Goldilocks amount of sugar»? | A bear's sugar bowl | Too much sugar | *Just the right amount, not too much and not too little | Nothing at all
